  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The given potentiometer has its wire of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>. When the sliding contact is in the middle of the potentiometer wire, the potential drop across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> resistor is:</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e2b416a9-3e57-44aa-831b-e9854e025c1b-image.png\" style=\"width: 279px; height: 165px;\" /></p>",
